[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) merged every date report into one issue, because the desk merges on the
subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)). Read by cause, the reports hold
more than one problem. Each one below has its own ticket, with the reports it covers.

## The problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

<Callout kind="warn">
Counts come from the desk's own rule in <code>src/lib/kb/causes.ts</code> and its notes in
<code>src/lib/data/desk-notes.json</code>, over the export of 4 October, built when the page renders.
</Callout>

### parser: the shared date parser

The shared parser reads every date month first, and every tenant on file writes the day first. A booking
for 7 April comes out as 4 July. This is the bug #4471 was opened for.

### hint: the booking-v3 date-field hint

Tenants on the booking-v3 form show `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field, so their people type the month
first, and the form reads the date the tenant's way, day first. Only reports sent through that form count
here. The desk's cause table marks this cause "not this ticket — no ticket of its own": #4471 was opened
for the parser. Fixing the parser does not fix these: the hint is wrong, not the parser.

### The one-day reports: an observation

The desk's notes list some reports as a one-day move. Its cause table files them under `parser` by tenant
and footnotes them, and so does the table above: they stay inside the `parser` count. That filing comes
from the tenant and the channel, not from what the reports say. Most describe a date one day off, or one
that differs by where the reader is, as in "Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday.";
none of their bodies describes a day and month swap. Nothing in the export says what causes them, and a time zone or day
boundary is only a guess. [#3](https://github.com/pavani06/s01e03-run2/issues/3) records them as an
observation.

## How to check

- The cause of a report is `causeOf` in `src/lib/kb/causes.ts`, never the intake tag, which guesses
  from the reporter's browser.
- The export repeats some reports across overlapping pages; each id counts once (`uniqueById`).
- The one-day reports are `oneDayMove` in `src/lib/data/desk-notes.json`. They stay under the cause the
  desk files them by (`readAs`), so the counts match the desk's cause table on [#4471](/kb/incidents/4471).
- Each ticket lists the ids of the reports it covers.

